version: "Cryptologia submission Revision 7A"
date-released: "2026-09-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ja9925ydbsu/Hill-Enigma-SPN-HESPN-COGGINS"
license: MIT
abstract: "Reference software and supporting materials for HESPN, the Hill Enigma Substitution-Permutation Network. The repository supports an order-eight rotor-scheduled Hill-derived byte-local SPN linear-layer construction, its implementation validation, and bounded analysis of its diffusion limits. The Enigma name refers only to public stepping among geometric matrix orientations. HESPN is a research harness, not a deployment-ready cipher, and no full-round security claim or comparative scheduling advantage is asserted."
keywords:
  - cryptography
  - Hill cipher
  - substitution-permutation network
  - matrix diffusion
  - rotor scheduling
  - branch number
  - linear cryptanalysis
  - differential cryptanalysis
  - HESPN
